data=col4,arch_icon_researcher_64px_easty
data=col5,arch_icon_researcher_96px_easty
data=col6,4
data=col7,6

// 2941
[dbrow_2941]
table=dbtable_91
data=col0,11
data=col1,4
data=col2,Simon Templeton
data=col3,Infamous pot-hunter. He's expensive, but has a lot of experience.
data=col4,arch_icon_researcher_64px_simon
data=col5,arch_icon_researcher_96px_simon
data=col6,6
data=col7,9

// 2942
[dbrow_2942]
table=dbtable_91
data=col0,12
data=col1,4
data=col2,Anna Jones
data=col3,One-time freelancer now going legit with the Archaeology Guild.
data=col4,arch_icon_researcher_64px_anna
data=col5,arch_icon_researcher_96px_anna
data=col6,6
data=col7,9

// 2943
[dbrow_2943]
table=dbtable_91
data=col0,13
data=col1,4
data=col2,Asgarnia Smith
data=col3,Four-time winner of the 'Archaeologist of the Year' award.
data=col4,arch_icon_researcher_64px_asgarnia
data=col5,arch_icon_researcher_96px_asgarnia
data=col6,6
data=col7,9
data=col8,1

// 2944
[dbrow_2944]
table=dbtable_91
data=col0,14
data=col1,4
data=col2,Elissa Giovanni
data=col3,Burgeoning expert in golems, constructs and automata.
data=col4,arch_icon_researcher_64px_elissa
data=col5,arch_icon_researcher_96px_elissa
data=col6,6
data=col7,9
data=col8,4

// 2945
[dbrow_2945]
table=dbtable_91
data=col0,15
data=col1,0
data=col2,Dr Nabanik
data=col3,An expert in Zarosian culture, with first-hand knowledge of ages past.
data=col4,arch_icon_researcher_64px_drnabanik
data=col5,arch_icon_researcher_96px_drnabanik
data=col6,8
data=col7,12
data=col8,3

// 2946
[dbrow_2946]
table=dbtable_91
data=col0,16
data=col1,0
data=col2,Vanescula
data=col3,Highly intelligent and knowledgeable, and keeps people on task.
data=col4,arch_icon_researcher_64px_vanescula
data=col5,arch_icon_researcher_96px_vanescula
data=col7,12
data=col8,5

// 2947
[dbrow_2947]
table=dbtable_91
data=col0,17
data=col1,0
data=col2,Movario
data=col3,Freelance relic hunter, with a great deal of expertise in magic items.
data=col4,arch_icon_researcher_64px_movario
data=col5,arch_icon_researcher_96px_movario
data=col6,8
data=col7,12
data=col8,2

// 2948
[dbrow_2948]
table=dbtable_91
data=col0,18
data=col1,0
data=col2,Gee'ka
data=col3,A one-time golem master for Armadyl, she's happiest when tinkering.
data=col4,arch_icon_researcher_64px_geeka
data=col5,arch_icon_researcher_96px_geeka
data=col6,6
data=col7,12
data=col8,6

// 2949
[dbrow_2949]
table=dbtable_91
data=col0,19
data=col1,0
data=col2,Zanik
data=col3,Expert on Bandosian culture, digging tunnels and working underground.
data=col4,arch_icon_researcher_64px_zanik
data=col5,arch_icon_researcher_96px_zanik
data=col6,8
data=col8,7

// 2950
[dbrow_2950]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,1
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_avian_player
data=col3,What an unusual find! This strange device plays back recorded sound from things call 'song eggs'. The audio is emitted from stylised baby birds sat in a nest.
data=col4,76
data=col5,obj_49630
data=col6,obj_49631

// 2951
[dbrow_2951]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,2
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_aviansie_dreamcoat
data=col3,This multi-coloured coat is very vibrant and distinctive. It perhaps suggests a connection between the aviansie and colourful mating displays by many types of bird.
data=col4,81
data=col5,obj_49632
data=col6,obj_49633

// 2952
[dbrow_2952]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,3
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_blackfire_lance
data=col3,This weapon is not unlike other lances our archaeologists have discovered, but attached to it is a device akin to a cannon barrel. At best this would provide a single shot.
data=col4,103
data=col5,obj_49634
data=col6,obj_49635

// 2953
[dbrow_2953]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,4
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ceremonial_plume
data=col3,Perhaps made to mimic certain bird plumage, this flamboyant headgear certainly attracts attention.
data=col4,81
data=col5,obj_49636
data=col6,obj_49637

// 2954
[dbrow_2954]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,5
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_chuluu_stone
data=col3,Research teams have pored over Howl's notes and believe this so-called chuluu stone's uses were as wide-ranging as an ingredient in alchemy spells and in producing healing potions.
data=col4,118
data=col5,obj_49638
data=col6,obj_49639

// 2955
[dbrow_2955]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,6
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_flat_cap
data=col3,Perhaps less fashionable than other artefacts discovered at Stormguard, but perhaps more practical, especially if worn while flying around in the strong winds here.
data=col4,111
data=col5,obj_49640
data=col6,obj_49641

// 2956
[dbrow_2956]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,7
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_golem_heart
data=col3,Golem technology is a process mostly lost to those of us in the current age. It appears golem production was at its height during the Third Age, and at Stormguard Citadel especially so.
data=col4,98
data=col5,obj_49642
data=col6,obj_49643

// 2957
[dbrow_2957]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,8
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_golem_instruction
data=col3,The instructions discovered with (or still being used by) golems that survive to the current day tend to be paper based. This device seems mechanical in nature. How strange.
data=col4,98
data=col5,obj_49644
data=col6,obj_49645

// 2958
[dbrow_2958]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,9
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_keshik_drum
data=col3,Music appears to have been very popular with the aviansie, even given what the site this was discovered at was used for.
data=col4,76
data=col5,obj_49646
data=col6,obj_49647

// 2959
[dbrow_2959]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,10
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_morin_khuur
data=col3,This odd stringed instrument produces a very distinct and pleasing sound. The head of it appears to depict some sort of animal, though it's unclear as to which.
data=col4,76
data=col5,obj_49648
data=col6,obj_49649

// 2960
[dbrow_2960]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,11
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_multi_scope
data=col3,At first glance, this device appears like a regular spyglass, but multiple pieces of coloured glass can be bent in front of the lens letting the user see things the naked eye cannot.
data=col4,85
data=col5,obj_49650
data=col6,obj_49651

// 2961
[dbrow_2961]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,12
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_night_goggles
data=col3,Aviansie do not typically have need to wear goggles while flying, according to site manager Gee'ka, but these goggles allow anyone to have superior vision in low light and even in the dark.
data=col4,111
data=col5,obj_49652
data=col6,obj_49653

// 2962
[dbrow_2962]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,13
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_parasol
data=col3,Fashion is abundant at Stormguard, which is odd given its purpose, but even inventors need to relax. Given how windy it is there, this parasol was likely more for show than function.
data=col4,81
data=col5,obj_49654
data=col6,obj_49655

// 2963
[dbrow_2963]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,14
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_pass_ikovian
data=col3,Gerege is an aviansie word much like 'pass'. These small metal ingots were used to communicate a person's rank or station, and could be used to gain access to secure areas.
data=col4,70
data=col5,obj_49656
data=col6,obj_49657

// 2964
[dbrow_2964]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,15
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_pass_stormguard
data=col3,Where the Ikovian gerege allowed us access to Stormguard Citadel itself, this Stormguard gerege may allow us passage into the site's more sensitive and secure areas.
data=col4,95
data=col5,obj_49658
data=col6,obj_49659

// 2965
[dbrow_2965]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,16
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_prototype_godbow
data=col3,It appears Howl attempted to make various weapons from aetherium, before settling on the godsword. Though aetherium is light, perhaps it was not suitable to make a decent bow.
data=col4,112
data=col5,obj_49660
data=col6,obj_49661

// 2966
[dbrow_2966]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,17
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_prototype_godstaff
data=col3,Aetherium alloy also works as a conduit for magical energies, so this godstaff seems a better approach than a bow, but presumably the more direct connection of a sword was more effective.
data=col4,112
data=col5,obj_49662
data=col6,obj_49663

// 2967
[dbrow_2967]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,18
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_prototype_godsword
data=col3,Here it is - a prototype version of the now legendary godsword. This weapon was constructed by the advanced alloy known as aetherium, smithed by the aviansie inventor Howl himself.
data=col4,112
data=col5,obj_49664
data=col6,obj_49665

// 2968
[dbrow_2968]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,19
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_prototype_gravimeter
data=col3,The team are unsure entirely what the purpose of this device was, but it seems to have a reaction to the gravitational core holding the destroyed remnants of Stormguard together.
data=col4,91
data=col5,obj_49666
data=col6,obj_49667

// 2969
[dbrow_2969]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,20
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_quintessence_counter
data=col3,Quintessence, according to some of Howl's notes found by our teams, was very hard to come by, hence the invention of this device to help track it down.
data=col4,118
data=col5,obj_49668
data=col6,obj_49669

// 2970
[dbrow_2970]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,21
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_razor_wing
data=col3,While an upgrade for the wingsuit, to provide some combat utility, we've advised against our archaeologists from applying them to their own wingsuits until we know more.
data=col4,85
data=col5,obj_49670
data=col6,obj_49671

// 2971
[dbrow_2971]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,22
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_shield_dayguard
data=col3,The Dayguard were one of the two tribes that helped to protect Stormguard from a direct assault (though there is no evidence that such an assault was ever made).
data=col4,95
data=col5,obj_49672
data=col6,obj_49673

// 2972
[dbrow_2972]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,23
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_shield_nightguard
data=col3,The Nightguard comprised of aviansie with better night vision and stealth capabilities. They were Stormguard's primary raiding force.
data=col4,103
data=col5,obj_49674
data=col6,obj_49675

// 2973
[dbrow_2973]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,24
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_songbird_recorder
data=col3,This device share some similarities with another device found at Stormguard, though seems to be more for recording sounds than playing them back, and in a much small form.
data=col4,91
data=col5,obj_49676
data=col6,obj_49677

// 2974
[dbrow_2974]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,25
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_spherical_astrolabe
data=col3,This three-dimensional astrolabe is a map of the heavens. Considering other artefacts discovered at Stormguard, this was likely used to keep track of various cosmic occurrences.
data=col4,118
data=col5,obj_49678
data=col6,obj_49679

// 2975
[dbrow_2975]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,26
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_toy_glider
data=col3,A children's carved wooden toy in the shape of some sort of glider, but with some bird-like stylings to it also.
data=col4,70
data=col5,obj_49680
data=col6,obj_49681

// 2976
[dbrow_2976]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,27
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_toy_golem
data=col3,This children's toy appears to depict an Armadylean golem, according to Gee'ka, but its proportions suggest a much larger variant than any she has seen before.
data=col4,70
data=col5,obj_49682
data=col6,obj_49683

// 2977
[dbrow_2977]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,28
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_beast_helm
data=col3,This helm is fashioned to look like an enraged beast of some kind, and is made with natural materials.
data=col4,94
data=col5,obj_49684
data=col6,obj_49685

// 2978
[dbrow_2978]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,29
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dorgeshuun_spear
data=col3,From what our consultant, Zanik, has imparted, the Dorgeshuun tribe splintered from Bandos in mid-Third Age. That spears of their tribal design are still found at the Warforge is curious...
data=col4,100
data=col5,obj_49686
data=col6,obj_49687

// 2979
[dbrow_2979]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,30
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_drogokishuun_sword
data=col3,These vicious swords have a hooked end, presumably for pulling enemies closer or sweeping shields out of the way, to open victims up to a follow up attack.
data=col4,110
data=col5,obj_49688
data=col6,obj_49689

// 2980
[dbrow_2980]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,31
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ekeleshuun_mask
data=col3,How strange! This oversized mask appears to be poking fun at the god Armadyl. Worn by goblins in the arena no doubt to amuse Bandos. Researchers are looking to see if any other gods were ridiculed by these big head masks.
data=col4,76
data=col5,obj_49690
data=col6,obj_49691

// 2981
[dbrow_2981]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,32
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_garagorshuun_anchor
data=col3,We are unsure if this anchor was a wielded weapon or simply used in the typical way. Staining around the walls of the Crucible suggest it may have been purposefully flooded for special events.
data=col4,97
data=col5,obj_49692
data=col6,obj_49693

// 2982
[dbrow_2982]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,33
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_high_priest_crozier
data=col3,A ritual sceptre would have been the primary use for this crozier, but it could have also substituted as a magic wand of sorts.
data=col4,89
data=col5,obj_49694
data=col6,obj_49695

// 2983
[dbrow_2983]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,34
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_high_priest_mitre
data=col3,This mitre would have been worn by a particularly devout follower of Bandos, or the Big High War God as site manager Zanik informs us he was also known as.
data=col4,89
data=col5,obj_49696
data=col6,obj_49697

// 2984
[dbrow_2984]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,35
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_high_priest_orb
data=col3,While more of a ritual item, this orb, with a small Kyzaj symbol atop it, could have been used to channel magic spells.
data=col4,89
data=col5,obj_49698
data=col6,obj_49699

// 2985
[dbrow_2985]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,36
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_hobgoblin_mansticker
data=col3,A rather simple sword, that seems best suited for skewering opponents.
data=col4,110
data=col5,obj_49700
data=col6,obj_49701

// 2986
[dbrow_2986]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,37
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_horogothgar_pot
data=col3,Zanik tells us the Horogothgar were infamous for eating their defeated enemies, including other goblins. Tellingly, the inside of this pot still holds an unpleasant lingering smell to it.
data=col4,119
data=col5,obj_49702
data=col6,obj_49703

// 2987
[dbrow_2987]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,38
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_huzamogaarb_crown
data=col3,Parts of this crown appear to share iconography with artefacts discovered at one of our other digs. This headgear was likely worn by a goblin tribe sold to the god Zamorak.
data=col4,104
data=col5,obj_49704
data=col6,obj_49705

// 2988
[dbrow_2988]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,39
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_idithuun_horn_ring
data=col3,Given where these were found, the team can only speculate that these rings were placed over the horn of a nosorog. They come in different sizes and colours that seem to stack in a pleasing pattern.
data=col4,94
data=col5,obj_49706
data=col6,obj_49707

// 2989
[dbrow_2989]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,40
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_kalikran_crown
data=col3,The Kal-i-kra, our site manager informs us, was a tribe of beings from which Bandos originated. This crown would have been worn by the tribe's chieftain.
data=col4,115
data=col5,obj_49708
data=col6,obj_49709

// 2990
[dbrow_2990]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,41
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_kalikran_mace
data=col3,Every side of this weapon has a different implement - a spike on top, a flat hammer surface, a bladed edge, a pick-like head and a 'tenderiser'. The team have dubbed it the 'switch army mace'. 
data=col4,115
data=col5,obj_49710
data=col6,obj_49711

// 2991
[dbrow_2991]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,42
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_kalikran_warhorn
data=col3,A nosorog appears to have been the original owner of this warhorn, which would have been used in the heat of battle for commanders to communicate orders to their soldiers.
data=col4,115
data=col5,obj_49712
data=col6,obj_49713

// 2992
[dbrow_2992]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,43
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_narogoshuun_ball
data=col3,A heavy rubber ball covered in spikes suggests the 'game' that was played with it was a dangerous one.
data=col4,76
data=col5,obj_49714
data=col6,obj_49715

// 2993
[dbrow_2993]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,44
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ogre_axe
data=col3,Considering the size, this hand axe-like weapon (that was styled after Bandos's 'Kyzaj' symbol) was likely wielded by larger creatures such as ogres. 
data=col4,81
data=col5,obj_49716
data=col6,obj_49717

// 2994
[dbrow_2994]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,45
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ork_sword
data=col3,This sword, while seemingly crude with its notched edge, is actually finely crafted and balanced. The bronze it is made from seems impressively strong, even when compared to iron or steel.
data=col4,81
data=col5,obj_49718
data=col6,obj_49719

// 2995
[dbrow_2995]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,46
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ourg_macuahuitl
data=col3,The name of this weapon loosely translates as 'mega hitter', or so our cave goblin researchers tell us. You wouldn't think glass fragments sandwiched between two wooden boards would be so deadly, but put it in an ourg's hands...
data=col4,97
data=col5,obj_49720
data=col6,obj_49721

// 2996
[dbrow_2996]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,47
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_rekeshuun_tether
data=col3,This strange contraption seems nothing more than a framework for chaining up to four goblins together. The metal bars are rigid and sharpened. 
data=col4,76
data=col5,obj_49722
data=col6,obj_49723

// 2997
[dbrow_2997]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,48
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_saragorgak_crown
data=col3,Considering most goblin headgear is constructed from reclaimed materials, these well-constructed and decorative crowns stand out. They sport a design reminiscent of Saradominist symbology.
data=col4,104
data=col5,obj_49724
data=col6,obj_49725

// 2998
[dbrow_2998]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,49
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_sculpture_bandos
data=col3,A hand-sculpted icon of Bandos, made with clay. The work is unrefined, but the end result is remarkably accurate to descriptions of the god Bandos.
data=col4,119
data=col5,obj_49726
data=col6,obj_49727

// 2999
[dbrow_2999]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,50
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_sculpture_kyzaj
data=col3,The Kyzaj shape of this crude clay sculpture is evident. It looks to be the same size as a recess in the back of the throne sat looking over the Crucible...
data=col4,100
data=col5,obj_49728
data=col6,obj_49729

// 3000
[dbrow_3000]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,51
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_sculpture_nosorog
data=col3,Nosorog are seemingly large, bulky quadrupeds with a giant horn on their snout. Research suggests these animals were brought here from another world, for goblins to survive against in the Crucible arena.
data=col4,94
data=col5,obj_49730
data=col6,obj_49731

// 3001
[dbrow_3001]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,52
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_thorobshuun_standard
data=col3,Each goblin tribe has its own symbol, rituals and customs. This Thorobshuun battle standard perhaps suggests this tribe was particularly martial.
data=col4,83
data=col5,obj_49732
data=col6,obj_49733

// 3002
[dbrow_3002]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,53
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_tower_cower_shield
data=col3,The team are not clear if this was a standard size shield (proportionally, for an ourg) or an oversized shield for goblins to cower behind. Considering Bandos, it was probably both.
data=col4,97
data=col5,obj_49734
data=col6,obj_49735

// 3003
[dbrow_3003]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,54
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_yurkolgokh_grenade
data=col3,What a strange contraption! Remnants of malachite and traces of water were found in two brittle clay chambers. It appears this was a thrown weapon that would shatter on impact and create a toxic cloud.
data=col4,83
data=col5,obj_49736
data=col6,obj_49737

// 3004
[dbrow_3004]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,154
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_spear_of_annihilation
data=col3,The fully restored legendary Spear of Annihilation. Speculation is rife at the Archaeology Guild that this might be the weapon Bandos used to ascend to godhood; however, there is no good evidence to support this.
data=col4,115
data=col6,obj_49965
data=col7,0
data=col8,0

// 3005
[dbrow_3005]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,0
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_training_sword
data=col3,On closer inspection, this is clearly just a replica of a centurion's dress sword, used for training prospective guild members. It makes sense to not entrust fragile, age-old artefacts to inexperienced hands. Still, it's a very good replica.
data=col4,1
data=col5,obj_49741
data=col6,obj_49742
data=col7,0
data=col8,0

// 3006
[dbrow_3006]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,152
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_tetracompass
data=col3,The origins of this artefact are unclear, but it appears to incorporate elements from the four main factions that fought in the God Wars. There also appears to be trace elements of a fifth faction, which brings into question the 'tetra' naming.
data=col4,50
data=col6,obj_49956
data=col7,0
data=col8,0

// 3007
[dbrow_3007]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,55
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_amphora
data=col3,These containers were primarily used to store goods for transport, both liquids and solids. Wine was the most common good stored within them.
data=col4,92
data=col5,obj_49743
data=col6,obj_49744

// 3008
[dbrow_3008]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,56
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ceremonial_unicorn_ornament
data=col3,This ostentatious ornament appears to wrap around a unicorn's horn. It is very beautifully crafted and adorned with small gemstones.
data=col4,48
data=col5,obj_49745
data=col6,obj_49746

// 3009
[dbrow_3009]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,57
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ceremonial_unicorn_saddle
data=col3,This ceremonial saddle suggests that unicorns were at least sometimes ridden. It seems unlikely that the icyene would use them as mounts, nor centaurs or lions, so it remains a mystery as to who might have done so.
data=col4,48
data=col5,obj_49747
data=col6,obj_49748

// 3010
[dbrow_3010]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,58
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_decorative_vase
data=col3,That this vase remained decently intact enough to be restored is testament to the craftsmanship that went into it. It was likely hand-made in Everlight's oikoi studios, from the local keramos clay.
data=col4,72
data=col5,obj_49749
data=col6,obj_49750

// 3011
[dbrow_3011]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,59
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dominarian_device
data=col3,This strange device, at least partly clockwork, has no immediately obvious mechanical use. It has stumped our researchers. It is, however, incredibly intricate and well beyond what was thought possible at the time.
data=col4,84
data=col5,obj_49751
data=col6,obj_49752

// 3012
[dbrow_3012]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,60
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dominion_discus
data=col3,This bizarre and intricate device is something of a mystery. Study suggests that it might be clockwork in construction, but what purpose it may have served is lost on us.
data=col4,61
data=col5,obj_49753
data=col6,obj_49754

// 3013
[dbrow_3013]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,61
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dominion_javelin
data=col3,While javelins such as this may have proved somewhat effective in martial combat, their primary use appears to have been in certain Dominion Games events. Likely they were used to showcase accuracy over long distances.
data=col4,61
data=col5,obj_49755
data=col6,obj_49756

// 3014
[dbrow_3014]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,62
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dominion_medal_bronze
data=col3,This bronze medal appears to have been awarded to third place participants of the Dominion Games. These metal choices seem to be the source of our own more modern competitive sporting events.
data=col4,69
data=col5,obj_49757
data=col6,obj_49758

// 3015
[dbrow_3015]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,63
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dominion_medal_silver
data=col3,This silver medal appears to have been awarded to second place participants of the Dominion Games. These metal choices seem to be the source of our own more modern competitive sporting events.
data=col4,69
data=col5,obj_49759
data=col6,obj_49760

// 3016
[dbrow_3016]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,64
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dominion_pelte_shield
data=col3,These wicker pelte shields appear to have been used in sparring, perhaps during certain Dominion Games events. It would have been completely ineffective in actual combat.
data=col4,61
data=col5,obj_49761
data=col6,obj_49762

// 3017
[dbrow_3017]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,65
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dominion_torch
data=col3,This artefact appears to be a variant of the more commonly hallowed lanterns, and channelled the magic of Everlight into an ever-living flame. It was presumably used as part of the Dominion Games.
data=col4,69
data=col5,obj_49763
data=col6,obj_49764

// 3018
[dbrow_3018]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,66
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_everlight_harp
data=col3,This stringed instrument, also known as a lyre, has turtle shell as part of its construction. Sea turtles have been spotted swimming off the coast by our archaeologists.
data=col4,51
data=col5,obj_49765
data=col6,obj_49766

// 3019
[dbrow_3019]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,67
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_everlight_trumpet
data=col3,While this instrument has a very simple construction, is is beautifully crafted and still carries a pleasing note.
data=col4,51
data=col5,obj_49767
data=col6,obj_49768

// 3020
[dbrow_3020]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,68
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_everlight_violin
data=col3,The more intricate of the instruments found at Everlight, this violin would have taken a lot of practice to master.
data=col4,51
data=col5,obj_49769
data=col6,obj_49770

// 3021
[dbrow_3021]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,69
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_fishing_trident
data=col3,This artefact suggests that icyene of old ate fish, which makes sense being they lived on the coast.
data=col4,84
data=col5,obj_49771
data=col6,obj_49772

// 3022
[dbrow_3022]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,70
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_folded_arm_figurine_female
data=col3,This stylised idol of a female icyene has its arms folded, presumably in some sort of reverential pose to the god Saradomin.
data=col4,56
data=col5,obj_49773
data=col6,obj_49774

// 3023
[dbrow_3023]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,71
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_folded_arm_figurine_male
data=col3,This stylised idol of a male icyene has its arms folded, presumably in some sort of reverential pose to the god Saradomin.
data=col4,56
data=col5,obj_49775
data=col6,obj_49776

// 3024
[dbrow_3024]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,72
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_frying_pan
data=col3,What these artefacts were actually named or used for is not something we've been able to discover so far, beyond their use in funerary practices. Vanescula came up with the term 'frying pan'.
data=col4,42
data=col5,obj_49777
data=col6,obj_49778

// 3025
[dbrow_3025]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,73
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_hallowed_lantern
data=col3,These lanterns could purportedly carry a spark of Everlight's magical power within them, providing a constant source of light. Unfortunately, we have had to substitute a simple candle in place of the magic.
data=col4,42
data=col5,obj_49779
data=col6,obj_49780

// 3026
[dbrow_3026]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,74
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_icyene_bowl
data=col3,Evidence suggests these bowls were primarily used for cleaning activities such as the washing of hands and wings. Residues suggest the water within them was scented with flower petals.
data=col4,72
data=col5,obj_49781
data=col6,obj_49782

// 3027
[dbrow_3027]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,75
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_icyene_cup
data=col3,The design of this cup is striking and distinctive and, though faded, depicts a scene on its side. The image on this cup looks to depict the light atop the main structure at Everlight.
data=col4,72
data=col5,obj_49783
data=col6,obj_49784

// 3028
[dbrow_3028]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,76
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_icyene_dagger
data=col3,Researchers wonder what use the icyene could have had for a dagger, considering they could fly and strike from a distance. Perhaps it was more of a tool than a weapon.
data=col4,100
data=col5,obj_49785
data=col6,obj_49786

// 3029
[dbrow_3029]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,77
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_icyene_lance
data=col3,The lance appears to be far less common a weapon for the icyene that the spear, likely because it would have required more specialised training to wield effectively, but also many of the examples we have found are on the ornate side.
data=col4,117
data=col5,obj_49787
data=col6,obj_49788

// 3030
[dbrow_3030]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,78
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_icyene_spear
data=col3,The spear was the primary armament of standard icyene troops, giving them both versatility and range, making great use of their ability to fly.
data=col4,117
data=col5,obj_49789
data=col6,obj_49790

// 3031
[dbrow_3031]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,79
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_icyene_short_sword
data=col3,Short swords such as this would primarily have been wielded by the hetairoi, icyene knights from noble families. While effective, they were a less dependable weapon for more martial forces, not taking advantage of the icyene's ability to fly.
data=col4,100
data=col5,obj_49791
data=col6,obj_49792

// 3032
[dbrow_3032]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,80
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_painting_athelete
data=col3,This painting appears to depict a much-loved Dominion Games medallist, but the scene itself is quite melancholy, perhaps in an attempt to convey humility or hubris. It's hard to tell.
data=col4,105
data=col5,obj_49793
data=col6,obj_49794

// 3033
[dbrow_3033]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,81
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_painting_everlight
data=col3,This painting seems to depict an aerial view of Everlight, showing the landmass more clearly than we can make out beneath the surface of the water now.
data=col4,105
data=col5,obj_49795
data=col6,obj_49796

// 3034
[dbrow_3034]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,82
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_painting_saradomin
data=col3,Here is a painting that depicts the god Saradomin in a particularly flattering image. The halo, or 'glory', behind his head denotes his divine stature.
data=col4,105
data=col5,obj_49797
data=col6,obj_49798

// 3035
[dbrow_3035]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,83
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_rod_of_asclepius
data=col3,Asclepius appears to be a figure from early icyene culture, according to research. There is some connection with him being a renowned healer or surgeon. This rod - a snake or worm twisted around a spindle - is also connected with medicine.
data=col4,92
data=col5,obj_49799
data=col6,obj_49800

// 3036
[dbrow_3036]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,84
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_scroll_of_scripture
data=col3,Translations of this scroll mark it out as a series of steps to achieve 'enlightenment'. Saradomin is namechecked frequently, but other words stand out, such as nectar and ambrosia.
data=col4,109
data=col5,obj_49801
data=col6,obj_49802

// 3037
[dbrow_3037]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,85
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_tablet_of_equations
data=col3,Markings on this stone tablet depict some fundamentals of mathematics, in particular geometry, algebra and references to something called the 'golden ratio'.
data=col4,109
data=col5,obj_49803
data=col6,obj_49804

// 3038
[dbrow_3038]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,86
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_branding_iron
data=col3,The design of this branding iron seems both familiar and not. Despite where this was discovered, it appears to have been used to mark cult members, so they could identify each other in public.
data=col4,45
data=col5,obj_49805
data=col6,obj_49806

// 3039
[dbrow_3039]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,87
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_chaos_star
data=col3,Researchers have so far been unable to determine what the style of this metallic design is supposed to depict, but functionally it acts as a dampener for chaotic energies.
data=col4,68
data=col5,obj_49807
data=col6,obj_49808

// 3040
[dbrow_3040]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,88
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_crest_of_dagon
data=col3,This is a highly unusual find, suggesting Star Lodge hides sinister secrets. The eye-like design of this crest is very unnerving.
data=col4,24
data=col5,obj_49809
data=col6,obj_49810

// 3041
[dbrow_3041]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,89
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dis_mask_lesser
data=col3,Members of the Order of Dis supposedly wore these masks during sacrificial rituals and other cult duties, to hide their identities. This lesser demon mask would likely have been for acolytes.
data=col4,29
data=col5,obj_49813
data=col6,obj_49814

// 3042
[dbrow_3042]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,90
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dis_mask_imp
data=col3,Members of the Order of Dis supposedly wore these masks during sacrificial rituals and other cult duties, to hide their identities. This imp mask would likely have been for neophytes.
data=col4,29
data=col5,obj_49811
data=col6,obj_49812

// 3043
[dbrow_3043]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,91
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dis_mask_greater
data=col3,Members of the Order of Dis supposedly wore these masks during sacrificial rituals and other cult duties, to hide their identities. This greater demon mask would likely have been for hyeraphs.
data=col4,29
data=col5,obj_49815
data=col6,obj_49816

// 3044
[dbrow_3044]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,92
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_hellfire_haladie
data=col3,Haladies are unwieldy weapons without significant strength behind them. This example has three blades pointing in different directions, giving lots of offensive and defensive options.
data=col4,98
data=col5,obj_49817
data=col6,obj_49818

// 3045
[dbrow_3045]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,93
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_hellfire_katar
data=col3,Sometimes colloquially referred to as a 'punching dagger', demon warriors would have worn these in pairs and put their considerable strength behind each stabbing punch.
data=col4,98
data=col5,obj_49819
data=col6,obj_49820

// 3046
[dbrow_3046]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,94
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_hellfire_zaghnal
data=col3,While it may look more like a tool, the zaghnal was effectively a pickaxe design refined into an effective armour-piercing weapon, though is technically classified as a warhammer.
data=col4,98
data=col5,obj_49821
data=col6,obj_49822

// 3047
[dbrow_3047]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,95
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_hookah_pipe
data=col3,Hookah pipes were often used in communal smoking dens, where groups of revellers could smoke flavoured tobaccos. The design of this pipe is almost hypnotic.
data=col4,20
data=col5,obj_49823
data=col6,obj_49824

// 3048
[dbrow_3048]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,96
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_manacles
data=col3,There is little to say about these manacles other than to comment on where they were discovered, that being in the Dungeon of Disorder's 'guest quarters'.
data=col4,45
data=col5,obj_49825
data=col6,obj_49826

// 3049
[dbrow_3049]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,97
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_opulent_wine_goblet
data=col3,Found in Star Lodge, this wine goblet is certainly extravagant. It is suggestive of the wealth of the clientele that the lodge saw fit to entertain.
data=col4,20
data=col5,obj_49827
data=col6,obj_49828

// 3050
[dbrow_3050]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,98
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_order_of_dis_robes
data=col3,The Order of Dis cult we've discovered were the seedy underbelly of Star Lodge. It is unknown whether the 'Dis robes' word play was intentionally knowing or just an unfortunate coincidence.
data=col4,36
data=col5,obj_49829
data=col6,obj_49830

// 3051
[dbrow_3051]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,99
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_painting_abstract
data=col3,It is hard to know what this abstract painting is trying to depict. Black is the most abundant colour, but there is vibrancy on display, and while chaotic in style, patterns also emerge.
data=col4,24
data=col5,obj_49831
data=col6,obj_49832

// 3052
[dbrow_3052]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,100
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_painting_infernal_source
data=col3,This painting is title the Lake of Fire, suggesting this may be an abstract image of lava. Is this a depiction of the Source or somewhere else?
data=col4,65
data=col5,obj_49833
data=col6,obj_49834

// 3053
[dbrow_3053]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,101
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_painting_infernus
data=col3,Movario informs us that Pandemonium is an alternate name for the Infernal Realms, the home of demonkind. The tapestry named for it is quite striking. 
data=col4,89
data=col5,obj_49835
data=col6,obj_49836

// 3054
[dbrow_3054]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,102
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ritual_dagger
data=col3,This wickedly snaking blade was most likely used for ritual sacrifices, likely upon the altar within the Dungeon of Disorder.
data=col4,36
data=col5,obj_49837
data=col6,obj_49838

// 3055
[dbrow_3055]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,103
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_metal_sculpture_lust
data=col3,While abstract, the research consensus is that this metallic sculpture represents two intertwined lovers. This was likely an ornament on display within Star Lodge, perhaps suggesting something about the lodge.
data=col4,65
data=col5,obj_49839
data=col6,obj_49840

// 3056
[dbrow_3056]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,104
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_metal_sculpture_possession
data=col3,The theme of this metal sculpture appears to be either control or possession. One figure seems to be manipulating the other.
data=col4,104
data=col5,obj_49841
data=col6,obj_49842

// 3057
[dbrow_3057]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,105
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_metal_sculpture_torment
data=col3,This abstract metal sculpture evokes two figures, one seemingly tormenting the other. It's very unnerving, yet still pleasingly aesthetic.
data=col4,89
data=col5,obj_49843
data=col6,obj_49844

// 3058
[dbrow_3058]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,106
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_spiked_dog_collar
data=col3,While the team have dubbed this a dog collar, it's clearly for a very large dog. Considering where it was found, the research team has suggested it was for a hellhound.
data=col4,68
data=col5,obj_49845
data=col6,obj_49846

// 3059
[dbrow_3059]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,107
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_trishula
data=col3,This trident-like tool, made from this area's hellfire metal, has been nicknamed the 'devil fork'. Perhaps demons used it to herd prisoners about the Source.
data=col4,104
data=col5,obj_49847
data=col6,obj_49848

// 3060
[dbrow_3060]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,108
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_trophy_chaos_elemental
data=col3,There are lots of trophies found at the Source, though this one was likely not on display in Star Lodge proper, given how alien and strange it looks.
data=col4,110
data=col5,obj_49849
data=col6,obj_49850

// 3061
[dbrow_3061]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,109
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_trophy_leopard
data=col3,Whoever collected trophies here clearly travelled far and wide to have bagged a larupia, given they are primarily found in the area now known as the Feldip Hills.
data=col4,81
data=col5,obj_49851
data=col6,obj_49852

// 3062
[dbrow_3062]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,110
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_trophy_lion
data=col3,Lions were understood to have been introduced to Gielinor by Saradomin, or at least most frequently fought alongside the icyene.
data=col4,81
data=col5,obj_49853
data=col6,obj_49854

// 3063
[dbrow_3063]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,111
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_trophy_wolf
data=col3,Why specifically a she-wolf was hunted is lost on the research team, however the trophies found where this one was come across as some sort of subtle warning.
data=col4,81
data=col5,obj_49855
data=col6,obj_49856

// 3064
[dbrow_3064]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,112
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_trophy_virius
data=col3,Another trophy not for public display. Virii, also sometimes known as blood reavers, are the chthonian equivalent of hellhounds.
data=col4,110
data=col5,obj_49857
data=col6,obj_49858

// 3065
[dbrow_3065]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,113
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_tsutsaroth_helm
data=col3,Tsutsaroth demons typically wear very little armour, and don't really need to make their visage more fearsome.
data=col4,116
data=col5,obj_49859
data=col6,obj_49860

// 3066
[dbrow_3066]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,114
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_tsutsaroth_pauldron
data=col3,Demons are not particularly well known for wearing armour, so why they would choose to protect their shoulders specifically is both odd and unknown.
data=col4,116
data=col5,obj_49861
data=col6,obj_49862

// 3067
[dbrow_3067]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,115
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_tsutsaroth_piercing
data=col3,There is much speculation as to where this piercing may have been placed by the tsutsaroth that wore it. Perhaps it was a mark of rank or achievement?
data=col4,104
data=col5,obj_49863
data=col6,obj_49864

// 3068
[dbrow_3068]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,116
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_tsutsaroth_urumi
data=col3,Urumi are an archaic type of whip, this one constructed from razor-thin hellfire metal. They were as dangerous to the wielder as any target. A weapon of terror.
data=col4,116
data=col5,obj_49865
data=col6,obj_49866

// 3069
[dbrow_3069]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,117
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ancient_globe
data=col3,Even as early as the Second Age, inhabitants of Gielinor knew it was a spheroid planet rather than a flat dimensional plane. The Zarosian Empire placed a strong emphasis on educating its citizens.
data=col4,118
data=col5,obj_49867
data=col6,obj_49868

// 3070
[dbrow_3070]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,118
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ancient_magic_tablet
data=col3,Whatever wordings or symbols once resided on this magical tablet have long since eroded, making its magic inert. There's now no telling what effect this tablet might have had.
data=col4,107
data=col5,obj_49869
data=col6,obj_49870

// 3071
[dbrow_3071]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,119
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ancient_timepiece
data=col3,An early form of watch, more akin to a portable sundial. Something like this would still have been quite effective and accurate.
data=col4,47
data=col5,obj_49871
data=col6,obj_49872

// 3072
[dbrow_3072]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,120
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_battle_plans
data=col3,These plans seem to capture the moment in time that led up the battle that caused Kharid-et to fall. It's likely this plan was concocted by the praetorians stationed here at the time.
data=col4,118
data=col5,obj_49873
data=col6,obj_49874

// 3073
[dbrow_3073]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,121
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ceremonial_mace
data=col3,Even members of the Zarosian clergy carried weapons, though it seems this mace was primarily for ceremonial uses.
data=col4,74
data=col5,obj_49875
data=col6,obj_49876

// 3074
[dbrow_3074]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,130
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_pontifex_censer
data=col3,This censer was likely used in various religious ceremonies to scent the air. Residue within might suggest they occasionally carried hallucinogenic compounds.
data=col4,81
data=col5,obj_49893
data=col6,obj_49894

// 3075
[dbrow_3075]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,131
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_pontifex_crozier
data=col3,This crozier is an example of what leaders within the Zarosian priesthood would have carried to show their rank within the church. This one is a relatively mundane example, no doubt from a lowlier member of the church.
data=col4,81
data=col5,obj_49895
data=col6,obj_49896

// 3076
[dbrow_3076]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,133
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_pontifex_mitre
data=col3,Mitres such as this would likely only have been worn by those highest in the Zarosian papacy, most notably the Pontifex Maximus, though how they fit them over the antennae is unclear.
data=col4,81
data=col5,obj_49899
data=col6,obj_49900

// 3077
[dbrow_3077]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,122
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_legatus_maximus_figurine
data=col3,A sculpture of Zamorak. Most samples we find of these are smashed beyond our ability to restore them. Presumably, the inhabitants had more pressing matters than desecrating such idols, and also little time to do so.
data=col4,25
data=col5,obj_49877
data=col6,obj_49878

// 3078
[dbrow_3078]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,123
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_legatus_pendant
data=col3,These pendants were carried by certain ranking members of the Zarosian military, as well as the custodians of this fort's carcerem. They effectively acted as passes into areas of high security.
data=col4,47
data=col5,obj_49879
data=col6,obj_49880

// 3079
[dbrow_3079]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,124
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_legionary_gladius
data=col3,The standard arms of a Zarosian legionary. While only a short sword, at the time it was the superior metal in comparison to other armies, and likely proved effective in combination with the standard shield.
data=col4,12
data=col5,obj_49881
data=col6,obj_49882

// 3080
[dbrow_3080]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,125
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_legionary_square_shield
data=col3,The standard defensive attire of an imperial legionary, the rank of file of the Zarosian military. Research suggests a cohort would lock shields in various formations when facing opposing armies.
data=col4,12
data=col5,obj_49883
data=col6,obj_49884

// 3081
[dbrow_3081]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,126
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_necromantic_focus
data=col3,This book - the Orconomicom, aka the Book of Orcus - was used as a magical focus primarily by praetorian guards, but seemingly some of Kharid-et's pontifex also owned copies. It primarily focuses on necromancy.
data=col4,86
data=col5,obj_49885
data=col6,obj_49886

// 3082
[dbrow_3082]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,128
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_painting_peace
data=col3,This painting appears to depict the primary meeting between Zaros and the Mahjarrat. This would have been a pivotal moment in the Zarosian-Kharidian War, something inhabitants of this fort likely partook in.
data=col4,74
data=col5,obj_49887
data=col6,obj_49888

// 3083
[dbrow_3083]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,129
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_painting_war
data=col3,This painting appears to depict a battle between Zaros himself and Tumeken, the leader of the Menaphite pantheon. The title roughly translate to 'Shadow of the Sun'.
data=col4,25
data=col5,obj_49889
data=col6,obj_49890

// 3084
[dbrow_3084]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,127
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_painting_legion
data=col3,This painting of the First Legion upon arrival on Gielinor, depicted here locked into combat with the divine hydra, Loarnab. Early evidence suggests this first legion was commanded by Duke Nemesis the Inescapable, a demon from Infernus.
data=col4,118
data=col5,obj_49891
data=col6,obj_49892

// 3085
[dbrow_3085]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,132
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_pontifex_maximus_figurine
data=col3,Dr Nabanik has identified this figure as a Mahjarrat called Azzanadra, the presumed leader of the Church of Zaros. The strange antennae on the head are found on many pontifex robes.
data=col4,74
data=col5,obj_49897
data=col6,obj_49898

// 3086
[dbrow_3086]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,134
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_pontifex_signet_ring
data=col3,These signet rings were used only by high-ranking members of the Church of Zaros, in order to access secure areas of the fort.
data=col4,58
data=col5,obj_49901
data=col6,obj_49902

// 3087
[dbrow_3087]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,135
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_portable_phylactery
data=col3,Our research suggests the praetorians carried these as weapons, each containing a demon soul. Once thrown at a group of enemies, the demon would steal a host and set upon the rest. The slang term for them was 'diabolus'. 
data=col4,107
data=col5,obj_49903
data=col6,obj_49904

// 3088
[dbrow_3088]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,136
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_praetorian_hood
data=col3,The hood of a set of praetorian robes. It's very heavy and well armoured, which is unusual for most modern magic users. They include a covering for the face, presumably for the sake of anonymity. 
data=col4,114
data=col5,obj_49905
data=col6,obj_49906

// 3089
[dbrow_3089]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,137
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_praetorian_robes
data=col3,While doubling up as religious robing, this gear's primary uses was as heavy protection for praetorians - warrior mages of the Zarosian Secret Police. It suggests their work was dangerous.
data=col4,114
data=col5,obj_49907
data=col6,obj_49908

// 3090
[dbrow_3090]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,138
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_praetorian_staff
data=col3,The standard praetorian staff appears to include a small censer, though for what reason is currently not known. We have made some finds that suggest a more ornate and powerful version of this magical staff existed.
data=col4,114
data=col5,obj_49909
data=col6,obj_49910

// 3091
[dbrow_3091]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,139
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_primis_elementis
data=col3,The term 'primis elementis' roughly translates to 'primordial elements'. We believe these totems were carried by each legion or cohort as a battle standard, and the loss of one was a source of great shame for a legion.
data=col4,12
data=col5,obj_49911
data=col6,obj_49912

// 3092
[dbrow_3092]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,140
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_spell_animate_dead
data=col3,The remaining legible text on this scroll suggests the spell written upon it was necromantic in nature.
data=col4,107
data=col5,obj_49913
data=col6,obj_49914

// 3093
[dbrow_3093]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,141
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_spell_ensanguinate
data=col3,This grisly little spell appears to steal the life force of an enemy and transfer it back to the caster. 
data=col4,86
data=col5,obj_49915
data=col6,obj_49916

// 3094
[dbrow_3094]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,142
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_spell_incite_fear
data=col3,From what we can make out, this spell's use appears to have been to freeze its target in place and/or cause them to rout. 
data=col4,58
data=col5,obj_49917
data=col6,obj_49918

// 3095
[dbrow_3095]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,143
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_spell_smoke_cloud
data=col3,While incomplete, we can tell this scroll would have caused a cloud of thick smoke to be conjured, though the smoke's effect is unknown.
data=col4,100
data=col5,obj_49919
data=col6,obj_49920

// 3096
[dbrow_3096]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,144
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_venator_dagger
data=col3,Venators acted as scouts, hunters and spies for the Zarosian Army, so travelled light, hence why they carried these daggers as standard issue arms.
data=col4,5
data=col5,obj_49921
data=col6,obj_49922

// 3097
[dbrow_3097]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,145
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_venator_light_crossbow
data=col3,The venator light crossbow was built for fast reloading to couple with the hit-and-run tactics that Zarosian scouts seemingly employed. 
data=col4,5
data=col5,obj_49923
data=col6,obj_49924

// 3098
[dbrow_3098]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,146
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_vigorem
data=col3,These glass vials appear to simply be an earlier form of potion container, though there isn't enough trace of whatever it once may have contained to identify it.
data=col4,100
data=col5,obj_49925
data=col6,obj_49926

// 3099
[dbrow_3099]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,147
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_zaros_effigy
data=col3,Finally, we have discovered an icon of the Empty Lord himself. No such icons have been discovered at the Varrock Dig Site, so we are lucky with how well preserved Kharid-et is.
data=col4,17
data=col5,obj_49927
data=col6,obj_49928

// 3100
[dbrow_3100]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,148
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_zarosian_ewer
data=col3,Ewers such as this were primarily used to store water making them incredibly valuable at this fort. This area was not desert at the time in which it operated, but was likely incredibly humid.
data=col4,93
data=col5,obj_49929
data=col6,obj_49930

// 3101
[dbrow_3101]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,149
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_zarosian_stein
data=col3,This tankard has a built-in lid, likely in order to keep the contents from contamination by insects and particulates. Some of those we've found contain trace elements of alcoholic beverages.
data=col4,93
data=col5,obj_49931
data=col6,obj_49932

// 3102
[dbrow_3102]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,150
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_zarosian_training_dummy
data=col3,This dummy, likely used to drill legionaries within the castra, are fashioned after what appear to be chthonian demons. Being the chthonians were also citizens of the Zarosian Empire, this styling comes across as an odd choice.
data=col4,17
data=col5,obj_49933
data=col6,obj_49934

