// 3713
[dbrow_3713]
table=dbtable_91
data=col0,20
data=col1,0
data=col2,Mr Mordaut
data=col3,An authority on dragons and the dragonkin, and expert natural historian.
data=col4,arch_icon_researcher_mr_mordaut
data=col5,arch_icon_researcher_mr_mordaut
data=col6,8
data=col7,12
data=col8,8

// 3714
[dbrow_3714]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,160
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_death_mask
data=col3,The team are not yet sure what factor determines if a dragonkin is interred in a coffin or cremated with their ashes stored in urns. Those interred, however, have these orgone-decorated stone masks placed over their faces.
data=col4,99
data=col5,obj_50708
data=col6,obj_50709

// 3715
[dbrow_3715]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,161
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dragon_burner
data=col3,This piece of scientific equipment generates a controlled flame for heating flasks. The little dragon head motif at the top makes it look like it is breathing out the fire - an interesting decorative detail not often seen with dragonkin artefacts.
data=col4,102
data=col5,obj_50710
data=col6,obj_50711

// 3716
[dbrow_3716]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,162
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dragon_scalpel
data=col3,Compared to scalpels used by other races, this one looks relatively grim and nasty - almost akin to an implement of torture - but given how hardy dragonkin are thought to be, it's likely necessary to pierce and cut their tough hides.
data=col4,101
data=col5,obj_50712
data=col6,obj_50713

// 3717
[dbrow_3717]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,163
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dragonkin_calendar
data=col3,This calendar doesn't appear to correspond with any current or known calendars, which makes sense given dragonkin civilisation predates our history. Researchers are trying to interpret it, looking for any doomsday prophecies.
data=col4,99
data=col5,obj_50714
data=col6,obj_50715

// 3718
[dbrow_3718]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,164
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_dragonkin_staff
data=col3,While not a weapon, this ceremonial staff could certainly still be used as one. It appears that, even in death, the dragonkin are prepared for a fight. They must have been through a lot as a species, and still yet survive.
data=col4,99
data=col5,obj_50716
data=col6,obj_50717

// 3719
[dbrow_3719]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,165
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_gold_dish
data=col3,'Dish' is a loose term for this contraption, which is predominantly made of gold. It is certainly not for storing fruit in, nor serving food. There appears to be a space for one of these atop the 'giant' golden pyramid in Xolo City.
data=col4,120
data=col5,obj_50718
data=col6,obj_50719

// 3720
[dbrow_3720]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,166
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_kilaya
data=col3,We've been unable to determine the meaning of the term 'kilaya', though we know this is what they are called from journals among other grave goods. It's akin to a four-bladed spike or dagger, but appears to be ceremonial.
data=col4,96
data=col5,obj_50721
data=col6,obj_50722

// 3721
[dbrow_3721]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,167
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_lingam_stone
data=col3,This smooth egg-shaped stone has a carving on it, though there is still speculation as to what it depicts. The competing theories are that it is either two dragonkin hands drawing in cosmic power or two dragonkin beneath a waterfall.
data=col4,108
data=col5,obj_50725
data=col6,obj_50726

// 3722
[dbrow_3722]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,168
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_master_control
data=col3,Elements of the design of this device suggest a similar function to dragonkin 'effigies', but also blends in elements of the 'pylons' occasionally discovered inside Orthen ruins. It appears that this device can be worn on the head.
data=col4,108
data=col5,obj_50727
data=col6,obj_50728

// 3723
[dbrow_3723]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,169
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_meditation_pipe
data=col3,The team believe the word 'meditation' to be somewhat euphemistic, going by analysis on the residues found in examples of these pipes. Indeed, one researcher's 'detailed analysis' had them seeing dancing pink dragons for a time.
data=col4,106
data=col5,obj_50729
data=col6,obj_50730

// 3724
[dbrow_3724]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,170
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_orthenglass_flask
data=col3,This flask, made almost entirely of orthenglass save for a small amount of dragon metal around the neck, has a very distinctive shape. Within some of those discovered, we have been able to take samples of ages-old potions.
data=col4,102
data=col5,obj_50731
data=col6,obj_50732

// 3725
[dbrow_3725]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,171
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_pasaha
data=col3,A translation for the word 'pasaha' still eludes us, but it is clear to see this is some sort of lasso. Given where it was found, this was likely used for the trapping and corralling of dinosaurs, and then also as some kind of leash.
data=col4,90
data=col5,obj_50733
data=col6,obj_50734

// 3726
[dbrow_3726]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,172
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_personal_totem
data=col3,Due to the totems some visitors to Anachronia have been discovering, it is speculated that this portable variant contained a small mote of the power that their larger cousins contain. It certainly shares some similar aesthetic designs.
data=col4,106
data=col5,obj_50735
data=col6,obj_50736

// 3727
[dbrow_3727]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,173
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_protective_goggles
data=col3,These goggles are clearly designed to fit a dragonkin head (we tested their fit on Mr Mordaut, who is the closest model we have). He informed us that the orgone-tinted glass ever-so-slightly corrected his long-sightedness.
data=col4,101
data=col5,obj_50737
data=col6,obj_50738

// 3728
[dbrow_3728]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,174
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_raksha_idol
data=col3,We call this an idol, but given the scale of the surrounding environment, it stands more as a statue within this model city. It seems to depict a particular nasty rex dinosaur. The team hope the real one was just as small.
data=col4,120
data=col5,obj_50723
data=col6,obj_50724

// 3729
[dbrow_3729]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,175
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_ritual_bell
data=col3,Given the dragonkin propensity for long bouts of hibernation, it is theorised that interred kin were left with these bells, in case they were wrongfully presumed deceased. Waking up from a nap inside of a tomb would be quite traumatic.
data=col4,90
data=col5,obj_50739
data=col6,obj_50740

// 3730
[dbrow_3730]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,176
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_singing_bowl
data=col3,These bowls typically contain a 'striker', which would have been run around the rim of the bowl to create a pleasing vibration - this being the 'singing' aspect. It would predominantly have been used in meditative practices.
data=col4,106
data=col5,obj_50741
data=col6,obj_50742

// 3731
[dbrow_3731]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,177
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_vazara
data=col3,We are unsure what the purpose of these vazara artefacts is beyond ceremonial. It presents as a club-like weapon, and has detailing that suggests it being both indestructible and unstoppable, but what if two vazara were to clash...?
data=col4,96
data=col5,obj_50743
data=col6,obj_50744

// 3732
[dbrow_3732]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,178
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_xolo_hard_hat
data=col3,This tiny (presumably) mining helmet has odd design elements, such as a vertical fluting at the rear and what seem to be eye holes towards the front. It appears to be made from reclaimed dragon metal, decorated with gold.
data=col4,113
data=col5,obj_50745
data=col6,obj_50746

// 3733
[dbrow_3733]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,179
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_xolo_pickaxe
data=col3,The team can only but presume these small tools were used as pickaxes by very small creatures. While there is only the one gold rock found in Xolo City, it would have been a relative motherlode to such a tiny people.
data=col4,113
data=col5,obj_50747
data=col6,obj_50748

// 3734
[dbrow_3734]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,180
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_xolo_shield
data=col3,This shield has a striking motif on its front, which looks to be a stylised salamander head with its tongue out (or perhaps spitting fire?). From the back, it seems to be at least partially constructed from a set of protective goggles.
data=col4,119
data=col5,obj_50749
data=col6,obj_50750

// 3735
[dbrow_3735]
table=dbtable_89
data=col0,181
data=col2,arch_icon_restoration_xolo_spear
data=col3,As with other Xolo artefacts, this spear also seems to have elements reclaimed from dragonkin objects. In this case, the base is a dragon scalpel, but it has been reshaped and then decorated with a gaudy amount of gold.
data=col4,119
data=col5,obj_50751
data=col6,obj_50752

