// 3780
[dbrow_3780]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,48
data=col1,2
data=col2,dbrow_3703
data=col3,Let Sleeping Kin Lie
data=col4,70
data=col6,We've stumbled upon many vats filled with dragonkin in suspended hibernation.
data=col7,On careful closer inspection, the team has determined that a number of tubes have malfunctioned, killing the dragonkin that were within them.
data=col8,4000
data=col11,115
data=col15,obj_49455,50

// 3781
[dbrow_3781]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,49
data=col1,2
data=col2,dbrow_3703
data=col3,Breath of Fire
data=col4,99
data=col6,Within the dragonkin crypt lies a sizeable funeral pyre.
data=col7,It appears that only dragonkin of a certain level of reverence were interred in ossuaries. Most kin that died appear to have been cremated instead, their remains left in urns stored in reliquaries also found within these crypts.
data=col8,4000
data=col11,115
data=col15,obj_50708,1

// 3782
[dbrow_3782]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,50
data=col1,2
data=col2,dbrow_3703
data=col3,Necropsy
data=col4,101
data=col6,The autopsy table found within the observation outpost is quite ominous.
data=col7,Further investigation suggests that the dragonkin were actually very conscientious and ethical before they were cursed. The outpost was a place of learning, not cruelty (though some on the team feel these two things are synonymous).
data=col8,4000
data=col11,115
data=col15,obj_50712,1

// 3783
[dbrow_3783]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,51
data=col1,2
data=col2,dbrow_3703
data=col3,Mind Your Head
data=col4,108
data=col6,A strange device sits at the heart of the Moksha ritual site - its purpose unknown.
data=col7,Study suggests this device could separate a person's mind from their body...assuming it ever worked. Archaeologists have been advised to take great care around this device (though in some cases, it might be an improvement).
data=col8,4000
data=col11,115
data=col15,obj_50727,1

// 3784
[dbrow_3784]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,52
data=col1,2
data=col2,dbrow_3703
data=col3,Xolo Dorado
data=col4,120
data=col6,Rumours of a hidden city of gold were not so unfounded, it seems.
data=col7,The model city built of gold within the ruins of Orthen is as mysterious as mysteries come. Archaeologists have been reporting tools going missing and think they keep hearing hushed whispering, but none of this is yet substantiated.
data=col8,4000
data=col11,115
data=col15,obj_50723,1

// 3785
[dbrow_3785]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,53
data=col1,2
data=col2,dbrow_3703
data=col3,Incomplete Portal Network I
data=col4,70
data=col6,It seems as though the dragonkin portal device is part of an entire teleportation network. Research should determine how to power up the connections to other locations.
data=col7,The teleportation device is clearly a combination of ritual magic and technology. It appears as though it is running extremely low on whatever magical energy is powering it. The team suggest adding some ancient vis to the destination device located at the observation outpost in the north east - it could work as a substitute magical resource.
data=col8,2000
data=col11,50

// 3786
[dbrow_3786]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,54
data=col1,2
data=col2,dbrow_3703
data=col3,Incomplete Portal Network II
data=col4,70
data=col6,Adding ancient vis activated an additional node on the teleportation network. Others however, remain inactive.
data=col7,One of the interns has a theory that the energy in the remaining teleportation devices is not refracting through the circuits correctly. The team feel that this theory may be worth exploring. It was suggested that loading up on orthenglass and attempting to correctly refract the energy circuit in a destination device may enable that destination on the network once more. The next logical device is located at the Moksha ritual site.
data=col8,4000
data=col11,50

// 3787
[dbrow_3787]
table=dbtable_90
data=col0,55
data=col1,2
data=col2,dbrow_3703
data=col3,Incomplete Portal Network III
data=col4,70
data=col6,Adding orthenglass activated an additional node on the teleportation network. The last destination however, remains inactive.
data=col7,After a long period of investigating, the team could not figure out what was wrong with the last remaining portal device. As a last-ditch suggestion, one young archaeologist suggested boosting the device with quintessence. They shrugged at you, and exclaimed that it worked at Stormguard.
data=col8,6000
data=col11,50

